{"exit_codes":[{"exit":"0","meaning":"the requested operation succeeded; for verify, checked and passed. Not a claim that everything referenced is valid","name":"ok"},{"exit":"1","meaning":"a check ran to completion and found something wrong: verify's comparison disagreed, a gate (hub check, pull) refused at least one object, fsck made a fatal finding, or a writer refused a request its check over the statements held decided (a rule the publisher named failing its bytes; a revocation that would undo itself), so holding more statements would not change the answer. What a gate admitted beside a refusal is still committed (pull) and said so","name":"checked and wrong"},{"exit":"2","meaning":"the invocation or the reader's own configuration could not be acted on: unknown option, malformed argument, unreadable or unparseable policy, no store. Nothing ran and nothing was committed","name":"did not start"},{"exit":"3","meaning":"contested, unknown, unchecked, unpinned, unsupported, an optional capability not configured, a reader limit, or a failure after work started","name":"could not check"},{"exit":"4","meaning":"the derivation names an input it did not pin","name":"nothing to re-run"},{"exit":"5","meaning":"the declared environment differs from, or is not available in, the one that ran","name":"environment mismatch"}]}
